{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-129028",
  "enisaUuid": "97619782-6c38-3369-a756-abf09565beaa",
  "description": "A vulnerability in the InstallShield file parser of ClamAV could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause a DoS condition on an affected device.\r\n\r This vulnerability is due to incomplete error checking when the InstallShield File Parser is performing a scan. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted InstallShield file to be scanned. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the ClamAV scanning process to terminate due to an infinite loop, resulting in a DoS condition on the affected software.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:31:40 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:45:58 PM",
  "baseScore": 7.5,
  "baseScoreVersion": "3.1",
